"""Local folklore, ecology and setting facts; no private engine instructions in public lore."""
from geography import NATION, SPIRIT

CREATURES = {
 'Yokai':'A varied category of uncanny beings, awakened objects and enduring local spirits. Determine an individual’s actual body, intelligence, origins and disposition; the category grants no uniform hostility, spell list or immunity. Authored Koma, Suzu-no-Ura, Oroha and Hagire keep their individual identities and bodies rather than becoming interchangeable encounters.',
 'Roadside Sparrow Imp':'A fist-sized charcoal-and-cream birdlike imp with a flat wooden-looking beak, bright bead eyes and a ragged red throat pouch. It steals soft sandal cords and nests beneath benches. Usually a mischievous nuisance that can be lured, traded with or driven off, not an automatic lethal encounter.',
 'Bamboo Fox':'A lean russet mana fox with green-black ear tips, a long brush tail and narrow pale eyes. It uses bamboo cover and a small misleading rustle rather than human speech or broad illusion mastery. Territorial animals can retreat, hunt or defend young; they are not automatically helpful pets.',
 'Moss-Tongue Kodama':'A small bark-bodied forest spirit with a round knotted face, dark sap eyes, two root legs and a long mossy tongue. It tastes rain and rearranges little offerings. Usually curious or mischievous; an actual polluted or damaged shelter can provoke it. It is neither a child nor a compulsory combat target.',
 'Antler-Moss Boar':'A dark bristled boar with pale rootlike growths over its brow and short moss-covered antler branches. It turns soft soil and follows fallen fruit. A fence gap, seasonal food and clear escape routes matter more than an invented grudge against all humans.',
 'Boundary Tengu':'An adult bird-featured mountain yokai with a long beaked face, dark feathered wings, humanlike hands and red-brown travel layers. It guards a particular claimed crossing and can bargain, bluff or fight. Wings and local knowledge do not make it omniscient or sovereign over every mountain.',
 'Cinder Umbrella':'An awakened paper umbrella with one amber eye beneath a scorched rim, a wooden shaft leg and a ragged tongue of warm ash. It hops, spins and spits small hot flecks, usually around abandoned shelter or mishandled offerings. It can be dangerous without becoming an explosive city-destroying artifact.',
 'Paper-Face Lurker':'A tall loose arrangement of old paper masks around a thin dark frame. One face turns at a time while folded paper fingers test doors and rails. It uses blind angles and limited decoys; the moving frame is real and can be pinned or disrupted.',
 'Scree Crab':'A low slate-shelled crawler with six jointed legs, two broad foreclaws and orange seam eyes. It wedges among stones and scrapes mineral surfaces. Falling debris and occupied crevices telegraph it; it is not automatically a giant quarry boss.',
 'Kiln Ashling':'A small round ash creature with a red ember belly, thin soot arms and a wide pale mouth. It follows hot waste and cools into a sleepy lump when deprived of heat. Newly licensed jobs use small weak individuals, not a spontaneous inferno.',
 'Crystal Centipede':'A many-legged dark centipede with glassy amber mineral plates and long jointed antennae. It follows seepage and vibrations through mine cracks. Its armored back has gaps between segments; driving it toward a supported side passage can avoid fighting beneath an unstable brace.',
 'Stone-Eating Centipede':'A heavy gray segmented cave predator with grinding mouth plates and pale sensing whiskers. It rasps tracks through soft seams and can undermine loose rock. Deep occupied galleries are optional dangerous ground; an ordinary miner does not inherit its level or tier.',
 'Storm-Kite Tengu':'A gray-blue feathered adult tengu with long kite-like wings, dark eyes and a pale hooked beak. Conductive ornaments rattle along its flight feathers. It uses wind and limited electrical releases around exposed ridges; it must land, see and recover like a real opponent.',
 'Whitefall Crane':'A tall white mana crane with black wing tips, pale gold eyes and narrow green-blue streamers trailing from its crown feathers. It inhabits water edges and makes short startling sound calls. It is a living creature, not automatically Oroha or a tame spiritual guide.',
 'Snow-Mantle Tengu':'An adult white-and-charcoal feathered mountain yokai with heavy talons, a narrow beaked face and a cloak of insulating down. It claims sheltered ledges, seeks food and can negotiate passage. Cold terrain familiarity is not invulnerability to every Ice spell.',
 'Ice-Reed Serpent':'A long dark aquatic mana beast with translucent reedlike dorsal fins, silver eyes and a broad flattened jaw. Its fins scrape across thin ice before its body rises. It hunts vibration and movement in cold water rather than appearing instantly on a refuge floor.',
 'Snowburrow Mukade':'A broad white-plated centipede with red seam markings and two long black antennae. It travels below snow over loose ground, leaving a settling trough and a dry scraping noise. A raised moraine or prepared hard platform limits its approach.',
 'Hollow War Armor':'An empty lacquered armor frame tied around a residual Soul working. Its joints creak and its head follows an old guard line; it may repeat orders or resist entry. Determine whether it carries a conscious spirit rather than assuming every animated frame contains a person.',
 'Paper-Face Moth':'A thumb-to-palm-sized ivory moth with ink-like spots resembling a little face and delicate serrated wing edges. It feeds on damp paper fibers and gathers near fresh paste. Most are nuisance wildlife, with small finite groups and ordinary practical countermeasures.',
 'Granary Rat':'An ordinary small brown-gray rat with dark eyes and a pale belly. It steals accessible food, hides behind shelving and escapes when threatened. Beginner jobs use one exposed weak rat at a time and practical gaps, not an elite swarm or compulsory disease outbreak.',
 'Whisper-Reed Oniwa':'A reed-bodied spirit with long leaf fingers, a hollow stem throat and shifting pale eye marks. It repeats a few heard sounds to draw attention into wet ground. Touch, observation and a changed route can expose its trick; it cannot know private memories it never encountered.',
 'Reed-Jaw Kappa':'A squat river yokai with dark green pebbled skin, broad webbed feet, a dull shell and a flat reed-fringed head basin. Adults have varied temperaments and can bargain over a real crossing; a powerful grip and water familiarity make a hostile one dangerous. It is not automatically a childlike mascot.',
 'Orchard Sootling':'A little black-furred round creature with enormous pale eyebrows, tiny paws and a warm amber belly. It hides among fruit baskets and licks sweet spills. Usually mischievous, easily redirected and not a disguised high-level assassin.',
 'Paddy Mudling':'A small wet clay body with pebble eyes, broad paddle feet and a sprout on its head. It blocks a channel to hold a comfortable pool. Moving water, a more attractive puddle or a careful physical removal can solve a nuisance without battle.',
 'Lantern Prowler':'A lean long-legged predator with bark-brown fur, two pale lamps of eyes and a split tufted tail. Its flank markings break its outline among hanging lanterns. Rustles and briefly reflected eyes give warning; it is not a free unseen opening critical attack.',
 'Root-Back Nue':'A heavy forest beast with a primate-like face, feline forequarters, a long scaled tail and pale rootlike growths along its dark back. It waits on overhead roots and attacks from a committed pounce. Its strange body is not proof of limitless abilities or a secret human identity.',
 'Mist-Lure Wisp':'A floating knot of pale blue light around a tiny dark seed. It repeats short heard calls and drifts above unsafe ground. The voice can be tested by echoes and line of sight. It does not erase a character’s recorded memories, move inventory or teleport the party.',
 'Marsh-Stilt Haunt':'A narrow spirit body balanced on four extremely long black reed legs, with a pale hanging veil around two golden eyes. It crosses deep marsh pools and probes close movement with its front legs. Dry raised ground denies part of its reach.',
 'Echo-Hide Stalker':'A low six-legged predator with slate-blue skin, a smooth eyeless brow and pale listening membranes along its sides. It hunts repeated vibration and can mimic a short sound. It has no private knowledge of the person whose voice it resembles.',
 'Empty Festival Husk':'An animated festival effigy with a hollow reed torso, torn bright cloth and a painted wooden face. A residual working repeats a limited procession or invitation. It may accept a properly ended ritual or need physical disruption; it is not every lost ancestor at once.',
 'Tanuki Wayfarer':'An adult raccoon-dog yokai with expressive animal features, a thick tail and practical borrowed clothing. Individuals may use modest Illusion workings and enjoy bargaining or mischief. They cannot create permanent money from leaves or automatically turn into any named person.',
 'Awakened Bell':'An old bell given movement and personality through a particular history. Its metal body, cords and chime establish its anatomy rather than an added human torso. A ringing interruption and petty mischief are plausible; authority over all spirits is not.',
 'Hush Crane':'A rare intelligent crane spirit with actual wings, long legs and an individual attachment to a place or agreement. Identity, disposition and history belong to the actual being. Oroha is the authored crane at its crossing; do not generate replacements with its name or role.',
 'Riftlimb Stalker':'Reserved anatomical classification for the unique authored Hagire: a towering woman-shaped forest yokai with two long arms, two long legs, a ragged split mouth and joints that can unseat and reset. Do not spawn copies or use this as a renewable random encounter. Use Hagire’s actual record, whereabouts, hostility and resolved condition.'
}

def add_types(w):
    added=[]
    for name,desc in CREATURES.items():
        if name in w['npcTypes']:continue
        w['npcTypes'][name]={'name':name,'vulnerabilities':[],'resistances':[],'immunities':[],'description':desc};added.append(name)
    return added

LORE = {
 'Akitsuhara — Country and People':'Akitsuhara is an inland Oni-majority country on Earth. Benitsuru is its capital beneath Mount Shiun; Mizuhara is the western lake town and Koganedai the eastern castle town. Humans, fae, beastfolk, dwarves and elves also live or work here. Farms, ferries, mills, public lessons, theater, shops and households matter alongside armed traditions. A native need not be a warrior, devout worshipper or servant of a great house. Ordinary residents wear varied, often vividly colored garments and patterns suited to their means and tastes.',
 'Akitsuhara — Shogun and Territorial Houses':'Shōen Kagetsuna is Shogun. His government coordinates common law, major roads and foreign agreements; territorial households retain substantial land, revenue and service rights. House Saionoma, led by Masazane Saionoma, has western agricultural and ferry influence. House Tsubakiri, led by Kureha Tsubakiri, holds the eastern town and sponsors imported equipment. Their peace is functional and fragile. A house includes ordinary relatives, workers and dissenters; neither ancestry nor employment establishes secret complicity.',
 'Akitsuhara — Local Justice and Foreign Visitors':'Magistrates hear real complaints and examine evidence; local watch officers handle public safety within their actual remit. A lord’s signature is not proof that a debt or accusation is true. Visitors can seek assistance and have obligations, but a Glowhaven office or guild badge grants no local judicial authority. Road robbery, coercive seizure and deliberate harm can have consequences. Akitsuhara has its own officers and custody arrangements rather than automatic transport into Glowhaven’s prison.',
 'Akitsuhara — Felt Forms of Magic':'Many traditions begin with felt mana: breathing, balance, rhythm, visualization and the repeated form of a practiced working. A teacher may ask a pupil to recognize the right sensation before explaining its structure. Scholars, experiments and analytical teaching also exist, and individual schools disagree. All established disciplines remain learnable under the world’s ordinary rules. The culture changes teaching and expression, not the four casting approaches or the need for actual training. Spell invention still calls upon Spellcraft.',
 'Akitsuhara — Visible Magic':'Practiced native workings often take flowing translucent shapes, with tapered edges and broad graceful motion. Water can unfurl in a smooth sheet, Wind in curling ribbons and Soul in layered drifting traces; other disciplines retain their own visible substance and hazards. Powerful workings can be spectacular, and an individual’s technique can be hard and abrupt. This tendency belongs to local training and culture across different species, not every Oni everywhere. Clothing and ambient light remain as varied as the people and places.',
 'Akitsuhara — Imported Mechanisms':'Magitech is a recent, uneven import pursued by selected houses, brokers and specialists. Most ordinary buildings, farming and craft still use familiar tools. Scarce engineered crossbows, swords and fitted armor can offer an expensive advantage, but require real components, charge, maintenance and trained handling. They are distinct from an ordinary enchanted object. Crossbows fire bolts and sword mechanisms support actual blade work; there are no guns. Some buyers seek military leverage while others hope for useful civilian tools.',
 'Akitsuhara — Samurai and Independent Rōnin':'Samurai traditions include household service, administration, escort, martial practice and personal obligations. Rōnin have no automatic common faction or moral alignment; some sell honorable service, some drift and some exploit the road. A foreigner can study a technique without acquiring a title. A sword, robe or proud introduction alone does not make anyone an official or a master.',
 'Akitsuhara — Shinobi and the Reed Veil':'Shinobi work includes observation, infiltration, message carrying, fieldcraft and carefully negotiated commissions. It is a profession and tradition, not a species or a new magical element. Yuzuri Kageura leads the independent Reed Veil Fellowship. Some groups serve houses and some refuse permanent service. Skill can be mundane, magical or mixed; stealth is not perfect invisibility and a commission does not erase its human cost.',
 'Akitsuhara — Shrines and Remembered Dead':'Local shrines maintain rites, community gatherings, practical shelters and particular spiritual boundaries. Belief and observance vary. Ancestor memory does not make every dead person available for conversation, and Soul practitioners distinguish an animated empty frame from a conscious spirit. The Maple Lantern Custodians cooperate without owning every shrine or speaking for all spirits. A living neighbor’s need can matter as much as a formal offering.',
 'Akitsuhara — Roads and Ordinary Travel':"Maintained roads connect Benitsuru, Mizuhara, Koganedai and the farming valleys; local tracks lead into more uncertain country. Ferries cross actual water, shelters give real refuge and the northern passes need preparation. A visitor can ask for the local guild, inn or shrine in ordinary words. Benitsuru’s guild means Adventurer's Guild - Benitsuru Branch, not a similarly named place in Glowhaven. A rumor or discussion of a destination is not a decision to travel there.",
 'Akitsuhara — Guild Branch and Expeditions':"Adventurer's Guild - Benitsuru Branch belongs to the same international Adventurer’s Guild as the Glowhaven branch. The actual Bronze, Silver, Gold and Platinum badges are recognized, and posted rewards are the amount received. Local work ranges from simple nuisances and deliveries to surveys, escorts and optional dangerous hunts. Foreign expeditions require actual travel permission and agreed fieldwork; browsing a notice does not accept a contract or issue a portal key. A field test, a guild commission and an academy expedition remain distinct undertakings.",
 'Akitsuhara — Trade and Everyday Costs':'Money is quoted in marks, the same unit used in Glowhaven and its partner lands. Grain, fish, timber, paper, lacquer, textiles and skilled work support the towns; imported mechanisms remain scarce expensive purchases. A plain meal commonly costs 6–12 marks, a shared sleeping place 8–12 and an ordinary private room 18–30. Agreed quality and circumstances can alter a quote. A household favor, rental or loan has actual terms rather than automatic free service.',
 'Akitsuhara — The Two Torii Routes':'The attended torii inside Benitsuru Portal Shrine is the authorized Evertree-network endpoint. Its fixed return leads to Evertree Base - Portal Room, and authorized route keys can be issued by the court or its actual transit delegates. Moonless Torii is a different old gate among Lanternwood’s lower roots. A restored local way bell can awaken it after a modest shrine repair undertaking. Once awakened, that route remains open even when the bell is elsewhere. Its far side returns to Moonless Torii, not the Evertree.',
 'Akitsuhara — Hagire and the Cedar Margins':'Hagire is the towering ragged woman-shaped beast reported along Ragged Cedar Hollow, Old Mask Trail and Foxfire Verge. Hanging strips and dry joint cracks warn of a sudden long-reaching lunge. She is hostile to travelers and their companions. The maintained roads, attended shelter and tended shrine courts lie outside her ordinary hunting ground. Survivors describe narrowing her approach beneath low roots and denying lateral routes; facing her unprepared is dangerous.',
 'Akitsuhara — Yokai among Neighbors':'Yokai include uncanny creatures, enduring local spirits and awakened objects with very different bodies and habits. Some are mischievous neighbors, some indifferent and some violently dangerous. An animal face or unusual body proves neither innocence nor guilt. Koma at Old Bridge Shrine and the argumentative bell Suzu-no-Ura are particular individuals, not the personality of every similar being. Local legends mix observation, custom and exaggeration.',
 'The Veiled Beyond — Mist and Living Wilds':'Beyond Moonless Torii lies a small fog-shrouded spirit wilderness. Giant cedars, dark marshes, white flowers, empty festival frames and immense half-seen beings give it a living but unsettling character. Some inhabitants imitate heard voices; others bargain or defend a particular crossing. Familiar sound does not prove a familiar person is present. Fog can conceal an actual path, not erase the existence of the return gate or transport someone without a journey.',
 'The Veiled Beyond — Refuge and Return':'Veiled Threshold has a dry approach and the stable return to Moonless Torii - Torii Court. White stones lead toward Bellroot Refuge. Real root paths connect the surrounding marsh, cedar hollows and festival road. Travelers can observe from the threshold, make a short visit or turn back without conquering the wilderness. Deeper exploration needs preparation; voices beyond the path may invite a dangerous mistake.',
 'The Veiled Beyond — Oroha’s Crossing':'Oroha is an immense intelligent crane spirit at the pale stream crossing. It dislikes being fed as a pet and negotiates limited assistance. It can be proud, helpful or obstructive without being a universal guide. Other cranes remain their own beings. A promise to return a message or restore a path has a particular scope, not automatic service or a permanent familiar bond.'
}

def add_lore(w):
    for name,text in LORE.items():
        if name in w['worldLore']:raise ValueError(name)
        w['worldLore'][name]={'text':text}
    # Reconcile the earlier groundwork with the author's explicit new direction.
    w['worldLore']['Oni — Arcane and Soul Magitech']={'text':LORE['Akitsuhara — Imported Mechanisms']}
